    "https://wsu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/WSU_Jobs/job/Spokane-WA/Teaching-Assistant-Associate-Professor---Career_R-15578": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant/Associate Professor - Career",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nOnline applications must be received before 11:59pm on: November 11, 2026 If a date is not listed above, review the Applicant Instructions below for more details. Available Title(s): 158-NN_FACULTY - Teaching Assistant Professor - Career, 159-NN_FACULTY - Teaching Associate Professor - Career Business Title: Teaching Assistant/Associate Professor - Career Employee Type: Faculty (+) (Fixed Term) Position Term: 12 Month Position Details: The Opportunity: Washington State University and the College of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences, Department of Pharmacotherapy invite applications for a Teaching Assistant/Associate Professor - Career Track faculty position on the Health Sciences campus in Spokane, WA . Expected start date for this position is January 1, 2027. The workload expectations of the position are teaching (80%), scholarship (10%), and service (10%). The ideal candidate will have a commitment to: teaching excellence; mentoring students from varied backgrounds; curriculum development and continuous improvement; contributing to the service missions of the college and campus; and developing and implementing didactic activities that foster excellence in our PharmD candidates, their pharmacy knowledge, verbal/written communication, and the clinical application of their skills in various courses. Additional Information: The screening of applicants begins Monday, November 2, 2026 . This position is a full-time (100%), 12-month annual appointment, with the possibility of renewal. This position is overtime exempt . 12-month Annual Salary Teaching Assistant Professor: $115,000-125,000 | Commensurate with experience and qualifications Teaching Associate Professor: $125,000-135000 | Commensurate with experience and qualifications In accordance with RCW 49.58.110 , the above salary reflects the full salary range for this position. Individual placement within the range is based on the candidate’s current experience, education, skills, and abilities related to the position. Successful candidates typically begin up to mid-point of the salary range. Benefits: WSU offers a comprehensive benefits package which includes paid sick and vacation leave; paid holidays; medical, dental, life and disability insurance package for employees and dependents; retirement; deferred compensation, optional supplemental retirement accounts. For additional information, please review the detailed Summary of Benefits offered by WSU for Faculty and Total Compensation . Required Qualifications for the Teaching Assistant Professor: Earned Doctor of Pharmacy (PharmD) degree Residency or Fellowship training, or equivalent experience in one or more of the following areas: teaching, general pharmacy practice, acute care, internal medicine, ambulatory care, or family medicine  Demonstrated experience teaching pharmacy courses with student-centered pedagogy practices, in both didactic and discussion-based formats Excellent communication skills and a demonstrated commitment to collaborating with diverse internal and external stakeholders Ability and desire to work collaboratively in a departmental setting Washington pharmacist licensure or eligibility to obtain Washington licensure within 45 days of hire date Must have, or be able to obtain by time of hire, a valid driver’s license and meet requirements in accordance with SPPM 7.10 and departmental driving standards Required Qualifications for the Teaching Associate Professor: Earned Doctor of Pharmacy (PharmD) degree and at least five years of relevant academic experience Residency or Fellowship training, or equivalent experience in one or more of the following areas: teaching, general pharmacy practice, acute care, internal medicine, ambulatory care, or family medicine  Five years of experience teaching pharmacy courses with student-centered pedagogy practices, in both didactic and discussion-based formats Demonstrated excellent communication and leadership skills and a commitment to collaborate with diverse internal and external stakeholders Ability and desire to work collaboratively in a departmental setting Washington pharmacist licensure or eligibility to obtain Washington licensure within 45 days of hire date Must have, or be able to obtain by time of hire, a valid driver’s license and meet requirements in accordance with SPPM 7.10 and departmental driving standards   Preferred Qualifications: Expertise/experience with patient-centered care and communication Position Sponsorship Eligibility: Not eligible for work visa sponsorship Area/College: College of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences Department: Pharmacotherapy Location: Spokane, WA The Department of Pharmacotherapy is one of two departments in the College of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences .   Application Instructions: Applicants must upload the following required documents to their online application. Application materials should clearly communicate how the applicant meets all required qualifications and additional requirements. 1) Resume (required) 2) Cover Letter (required) External candidates , upload all documents in the “Application Document” section of your application. Current WSU Employees (internal candidates) , before starting your Workday application, please use these instructions to update your education and experience in your worker profile in Workday . Internal candidates, upload all documents in the “Resume/Cover Letter” section of your application. Documents may be submitted as one file or separate files. Applicants are encouraged to upload as a PDF, if possible. Reference contact information will be requested later in the recruitment process through Workday. Background Check: This position has been designated by the department to require a background check because it requires access to children or vulnerable adults as defined by RCW 74.34 , engages in law enforcement, requires security clearance, interacts with WSU students in a counseling or advising capacity, has access to personal identifying and/or financial information, unsupervised access to university buildings/property, or other business-related need. A background check will not be completed until an initial determination of qualification for employment has been made. Time Type: Full time Washington State University encourages all qualified candidates to apply, including members of the military and veterans, and persons with disabilities. WSU employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must show employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. WSU is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact Human Resource Services: 509-335-4521 (v), Washington State TDD Relay Service: Voice Callers: 1-800-833-6384; TDD Callers: 1-800-833-6388, 509-335-1259(f), or hrs@wsu.edu . Notice of Non-Discrimination In matters of admission, employment, housing or services, or in the educational programs or activities it operates, WSU does not discriminate or permit discrimination by any member of its community against any individual on the basis of sex, race, color, national or ethnic origin, physical disability, mental disability, sensory disability, use of a trained service animal, age, religion, creed, genetic information, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, protected veteran status, honorably discharged veteran, member of the military, or immigration or citizenship status except as authorized by federal or state law, regulation, or government contract. Inquiries about the application of federal and state laws and regulations (including inquiries regarding the application of Title IX, ADA/Section 504, and implementing regulations), as well as reports and complaints of discrimination and harassment, can be made verbally or in writing to WSU’s Compliance and Civil Rights, the Department of Education’s Office of Civil Rights, or both. More information, resources, and contact information are available here: https://ccr.wsu.edu/notice-of-nondiscrimination/"
    },
    "https://wsu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/WSU_Jobs/job/Spokane-WA/Clinical-Assistant-Associate-Professor---MultiCare-Deaconess-Hospital_R-15577": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor | MultiCare Deaconess Hospital",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nOnline applications must be received before 11:59pm on: November 11, 2026 If a date is not listed above, review the Applicant Instructions below for more details. Available Title(s): 164-NN_FACULTY - Clinical Assistant Professor - Career, 165-NN_FACULTY - Clinical Associate Professor - Career Business Title: Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor | MultiCare Deaconess Hospital Employee Type: Faculty (+) (Fixed Term) Position Term: 12 Month Position Details: The Opportunity: Washington State University and the College of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences invite applications for a 12-month, full-time, annual, non-tenure Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor position located at Washington State University in Spokane, Washington . The clinical site for this position is the MultiCare Deaconess Hospital in Spokane. This appointment is a one-year renewable term beginning January 1, 2027.   Individuals with a strong commitment to an academic career and an interest in working at an innovative practice site are encouraged to apply. Time and effort for this position will be split approximately 50/50 between on-campus activities at WSU Spokane and practice site activities at MultiCare Deaconess Hospital. Responsibilities include:  Diabetes-focused patient care in an innovative transitions-of-care practice Development of a program of clinical scholarship and disseminate work through appropriate professional venues Supervision of pharmacy students during clinical rotations Didactic instruction Additional Information: The screening of applicants begins Monday, November 2, 2026 . This is a full time (100%), 12-month annual appointment . This position is overtime exempt . 12-month Annual Salary Clinical Assistant Professor: $120,000-128,000 | Commensurate with experience and qualifications Clinical Associate Professor: $128,000-138,000 | Commensurate with experience and qualifications In accordance with RCW 49.58.110 , the above salary reflects the full salary range for this position. Individual placement within the range is based on the candidate’s current experience, education, skills, and abilities related to the position. Successful candidates typically begin up to mid-point of the salary range. Benefits: WSU offers a comprehensive benefits package which includes paid sick and vacation leave; paid holidays; medical, dental, life and disability insurance package for employees and dependents; retirement; deferred compensation, optional supplemental retirement accounts. For additional information, please review the detailed Summary of Benefits offered by WSU for Faculty and Total Compensation . Required Qualifications for the Clinical Assistant Professor: Candidates must possess an earned Doctor of Pharmacy (PharmD) degree and have completed a post-graduate year one (PGY1) residency or equivalent training/experience. Washington pharmacist licensure or eligibility to obtain Washington licensure within 45 days of hire date. Required Qualifications for the Clinical Associate Professor: Candidates must possess an earned Doctor of Pharmacy (PharmD) degree and at least five years of relevant academic clinical experience.  Washington pharmacist licensure or eligibility to obtain Washington licensure within 45 days of hire date. Position Specific Qualifications for either rank (prior completion or within 30 days of hire): Strong communication and collaboration skills Blood borne pathogen training BLS for Healthcare Providers APhA or WSPA immunization certificate Completion of mandatory WSU training as outlined by the university and the department CITI training recommended (WSU IRB) Must have, or be able to obtain by time of hire, a valid driver’s license and meet requirements in accordance with SPPM 7.10 and departmental driving standards Preferred Qualifications: Experience precepting and evaluating student pharmacy candidates in clinical settings Experience teaching pharmacy courses with student-centered pedagogy practices, in both didactic and discussion-based formats Position Sponsorship Eligibility: Not eligible for work visa sponsorship Area/College: College of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences Department: Pharmacotherapy Location: Spokane, WA The Department of Pharmacotherapy is one of two departments in the College of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences .   Site: The clinical practice associated with this position would have a focus on transitions of care. This work would include the development, institution, and assessment of interventions whose goals are to improve the quality of care and lower rates of hospital readmission within the MultiCare system in Spokane. Founded in 1896, MultiCare Deaconess Hospital has a legacy of providing outstanding care to the Inland Northwest. This 388-bed facility offers high-quality inpatient, outpatient, diagnostic imaging, medical, surgical and emergency services. As an acute care hospital, we have a Level III Trauma Center, a Certified Chest Pain Center, a Certified Total Joint Restoration Center, an accredited Primary Stroke Center and is the only hospital in the area to be nationally accredited in bariatric surgery. Deaconess also features a Maternal Fetal Medicine program and Level III Neonatal Intensive Care Unit. Application Instructions: Applicants must upload the following required documents to their online application. Application materials should clearly communicate how the applicant meets all required qualifications and additional requirements. 1) Resume (required) 2) Cover Letter (required) External candidates , upload all documents in the “Application Document” section of your application. Current WSU Employees (internal candidates) , before starting your Workday application, please use these instructions to update your education and experience in your worker profile in Workday . Internal candidates, upload all documents in the “Resume/Cover Letter” section of your application. Documents may be submitted as one file or separate files. Applicants are encouraged to upload as a PDF, if possible. Reference contact information will be requested later in the recruitment process through Workday. Background Check: This position has been designated by the department to require a background check because it requires access to children or vulnerable adults as defined by RCW 74.34 , engages in law enforcement, requires security clearance, interacts with WSU students in a counseling or advising capacity, has access to personal identifying and/or financial information, unsupervised access to university buildings/property, or other business-related need. A background check will not be completed until an initial determination of qualification for employment has been made. Time Type: Full time Washington State University encourages all qualified candidates to apply, including members of the military and veterans, and persons with disabilities. WSU employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must show employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. WSU is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact Human Resource Services: 509-335-4521 (v), Washington State TDD Relay Service: Voice Callers: 1-800-833-6384; TDD Callers: 1-800-833-6388, 509-335-1259(f), or hrs@wsu.edu . Notice of Non-Discrimination In matters of admission, employment, housing or services, or in the educational programs or activities it operates, WSU does not discriminate or permit discrimination by any member of its community against any individual on the basis of sex, race, color, national or ethnic origin, physical disability, mental disability, sensory disability, use of a trained service animal, age, religion, creed, genetic information, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, protected veteran status, honorably discharged veteran, member of the military, or immigration or citizenship status except as authorized by federal or state law, regulation, or government contract. Inquiries about the application of federal and state laws and regulations (including inquiries regarding the application of Title IX, ADA/Section 504, and implementing regulations), as well as reports and complaints of discrimination and harassment, can be made verbally or in writing to WSU’s Compliance and Civil Rights, the Department of Education’s Office of Civil Rights, or both. More information, resources, and contact information are available here: https://ccr.wsu.edu/notice-of-nondiscrimination/"
